19387      /* STAT-SURVEYFREQ-009: SURVEYFREQ — Degrees of Freedom / Coefficient of Variation / Design Effect
19388       * Source: S154 / Chapter 118 / `Degrees of Freedom` (PDF p. 9650); S154 / Chapter 118 / `Coefficient of Variation` (PDF pp. 9650–9651); S154 /
19388    ! Chapter 118 / `Design Effect` (PDF pp. 9651–9652).
19389       * Discriminates: Verified default procedure context
19390       */
19391      options nosyntaxcheck obs=max firstobs=1 nodate nonumber nocenter linesize=160 pagesize=max nostimer nofullstimer validvarname=v7
19391    ! validmemname=compatible locale=en_US;
19392      %let syscc=0;
19393      title; footnote;
19394      ods _all_ close;
19395      ods listing gpath="%sysfunc(pathname(work))";
19396      ods graphics off;
19397      proc datasets library=work kill nolist;
NOTE: Deleting WORK.REGSTRY (memtype=ITEMSTOR).
NOTE: File WORK.REGSTRY (memtype=ITEMSTOR) cannot be deleted because it is in use.
NOTE: Deleting WORK.SASGOPT (memtype=CATALOG).
NOTE: File WORK.SASGOPT (memtype=CATALOG) cannot be deleted because it is in use.
NOTE: Deleting WORK.SURVEY (memtype=DATA).
NOTE: Deleting WORK.TEMPLAT (memtype=ITEMSTOR).
NOTE: File WORK.TEMPLAT (memtype=ITEMSTOR) cannot be deleted because it is in use.
19397    !                                         quit;


19398      ods path work.templat(update) sashelp.tmplmst(read);
19399      
19400      data survey;
19401      do state=1 to 2;
19402      do school=1 to 4;
19403      do id=1 to 6;
19404      response=1+mod(id+school,3);
19405      schooltype=1+mod(school,2);
19406      samplingweight=2+state+school/10;
19407      output;
19408      end;
19409      end;
19410      end;
19411      run;

NOTE: The data set WORK.SURVEY has 48 observations and 6 variables.

19412      proc surveyfreq data=survey;
19413      strata state;
19414      cluster school;
19415      weight samplingweight;
19416      tables schooltype*response / row chisq;
19417      run;

NOTE: The Rao-Scott chi-square test cannot be computed for the table of schooltype by response because the design correction is not positive.
NOTE: The PROCEDURE SURVEYFREQ printed page 1385.

